> **Farzana's take:** Every time I see a buyer choose D-VS2 over F-VVS1 in an Asscher, I want to stop them. The D color looks identical to F in a step cut — color only shows at the girdle edges in good light. But VS2 inclusions in a step cut show everywhere, all the time. The certificate grade that matters in an Asscher is clarity, not color. Prioritize in that order.

