## The Art Deco Lock

The Asscher cut was created by Joseph Asscher in Amsterdam in 1902. It arrived at the peak of the Art Deco movement, and everything about its geometry was designed for that era's aesthetic vocabulary: octagonal outlines, stepped concentric facets, geometric symmetry, architectural precision.

The Art Deco Lock is what happens when you pair an Asscher stone with an Art Deco setting. The stone's octagonal crown aligns with the geometric ornament of the ring — milgrain edges echo the step facets, filigree arches mirror the crown facets, angular prong heads line up with the eight beveled corners. The whole piece reads as intentional.

The stone and the setting were made for each other because, historically, they were. This is not a stylistic preference — it is a design match with 124 years of proof behind it.

The opposite of the Art Deco Lock is a modern minimalist setting with thin prongs and a plain band. It is not wrong — but it leaves the Asscher's character unexpressed. You paid for a 1902 geometric masterpiece and dressed it in a 2015 plain solitaire.

The Art Deco setting does not cost more. The [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis in white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-fleur-de-lis-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is [$1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-fleur-de-lis-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The [Diamond Filigree Vintage in platinum](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/diamond-filigree-vintage-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-304462?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is [$2,275](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/diamond-filigree-vintage-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-304462?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Both are less than a [plain cathedral solitaire in platinum](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-knife-edge-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311250?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$1,400](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-knife-edge-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311250?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

Put the Art Deco setting on the Asscher. The geometry locks. The ring looks designed, not assembled.

