**Verdict:** The lab 2ct D-FL ring at $7,600 (Art Deco platinum build) is one of the best value propositions in all of fine jewelry. A natural 2ct Asscher at comparable specs starts at $24,000. The lab ring at $7,600 is 68% less. The only thing missing is the natural origin story.

> **Farzana's take:** Asscher cut lab-growns are the most convincing lab diamonds I have ever evaluated. The step cut does not have the same light-scattering opacity as a brilliant cut — but that is the point. The Hall of Mirrors is an orderly, geometric light show, not a chaotic fire display. And orderly, geometric light does not distinguish between natural and lab origin. You cannot look into the table of a well-cut D-IF lab Asscher and see anything that tells you it is not natural. I have tested this on buyers. They cannot tell. The microscope can. Their eye cannot.

