## Asscher vs Emerald Cut Engagement Ring — Price and Face-Up Comparison

Many buyers choose between the Asscher and the emerald cut. Both are step cuts with the same clarity requirements.

The key differences are face-up size and shape personality. These two things drive different buyers to each cut.

| Feature | Asscher Cut | Emerald Cut | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|
| Shape | Octagonal (square with corners) | Rectangular (elongated) | Asscher sits square on the finger; emerald runs finger-length |
| Face-up size per carat | ~4.5 mm at 1ct | ~6.6×4.6 mm at 1ct | Emerald shows 25–30% more face-up area per carat |
| Clarity floor | VVS2 mandatory | VS1 acceptable (some VS2) | Asscher's parallel facets show more than emerald's offset facets |
| Entry natural 1ct price | [$2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Approx. $2,100–$2,500 | Similar natural 1ct pricing at equivalent grades |
| Entry lab 1.5ct price | [$2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Approx. $2,400–$2,900 | Comparable lab pricing between cuts |
| Best setting | Art Deco / vintage / 8-prong | Solitaire / pavé / bezel | Setting compatibility differs — Asscher rewards ornament |
| Personality | Geometric, vintage, architectural | Linear, modern, bold | Different aesthetic character entirely |

**Verdict:** If you want more face-up size per dollar, the [emerald cut diamond engagement ring](/emerald-cut-diamond-engagement-rings) wins. If you want the octagonal vintage aesthetic of the Art Deco era, the Asscher wins. Both cuts need VVS2+ clarity in natural stones. Choose by shape preference, not price.

